model {
  solo_operator = actor "Solo maintainer / store operator" {
    summary "The single owner who ships CWS listings, runs the admin licence portal, manages Stripe prices and produces store artwork."
    description '''
      The product is run by one person, so the repo treats operator workflows as first-class product surface rather than incidental tooling.
      
      This persona reviews licences and revenue in the Google-OAuth-gated admin portal, issues discount codes, resets a customer to free state during E2E testing, bumps manifest versions, and drives five separate Chrome Web Store submissions.
      
      Evidence (no file anchor, per actor rules): CLAUDE.md opens with a standing instruction to keep the README "Chrome Web Store Launch Status" table current per extension and version, and documents Stripe CLI operations plus an ordered D1 licence-cleanup runbook; docs/cws-submission-process.md covers store submission; the admin area under packages/landing-shared/src/admin and the admin API routes (licences, stats, discount codes, session, logout) are built for exactly one privileged operator identified by an ADMIN_EMAIL environment variable.
    '''
  }
  web_reader = actor "General web dark-mode user" {
    summary "Browser user who wants every site dark, currently served by Dark Reader or Night Eye, targeted by Browse Darkly."
    description '''
      The expansion persona beyond Google Workspace. Wants one toggle that darkens arbitrary sites, remembers per-site choices, and does not slow the browser down.
      
      Evidence (no file anchor, per actor rules): docs/browse-darkly-plan.md sizes this market (~1.2B dark-mode Chrome users vs ~12M served by existing extensions) and lists the incumbent weaknesses it targets - Dark Reader's measured Speedometer slowdown, developer-style brightness/contrast sliders instead of curated presets, cramped popup UI, and monetisation backlash. The Browse Darkly manifest expresses the same promise in store copy ("Dark mode for every website - beautiful presets, per-site memory, and smart detection") and grants all-urls host permission plus a sidePanel surface, which is the UI answer to the "cramped popup" complaint.
    '''
  }
  workspace_user = actor "Google Workspace power user" {
    summary "Knowledge worker who spends the day in Gmail, Sheets and Docs and wants a dark mode Google does not ship properly."
    description '''
      The primary paying persona. Buys one app (Gmail, Sheets or Docs) or the Suite bundle covering all four Google surfaces, then configures theme mode and preset from inside the host app rather than a separate options page.
      
      Cares about correctness under inversion: the Sheets "Preserve Grid Colors" and Docs "Preserve Page Colors" toggles exist for this person, because a spreadsheet whose cell fills are wrong is worse than no dark mode at all.
      
      Evidence (no file anchor, per actor rules): the store descriptions in each extension manifest name the audience directly ("Dark mode for Gmail with OS theme sync, sunset scheduling... Settings right inside Gmail"); README "Extensions In Depth" documents the per-app preserve toggles; the pricing surface in the shared landing components (Pricing / ProductCard / SubscribeContent) sells individual apps alongside the bundle; docs/darkly-suite-single-app-plans.md quotes $0.99/$5.99/$9.99 for a single app and $1.99/$9.99/$19.99 for the Suite; the customer account portal under packages/landing-shared/src/account lets this persona manage their own subscription after purchase.
    '''
  }
  darkly_suite_product = system "Darkly Suite" {
    technology "TypeScript, pnpm workspaces, webpack 5, React, Chrome MV3, Vite, Cloudflare Pages + D1, Stripe"
    summary "Five Chrome extensions bringing dark mode to Gmail, Sheets, Docs, Drive and the whole web, sold through one Stripe/D1 licence backend."
    description '''
      The whole commercial product line, built as a pnpm workspace monorepo.
      
      One shared engine (`@darkly/core`) supplies the theme engine, preference storage, payment client, settings UI and conflict detection; per-site plugins (`@darkly/site-gmail|sheets|docs|drive|generic`) add the host-app specifics; five thin extension packages compose them into shippable MV3 builds.
      
      The monorepo exists **because the suite sells five separately-licensed products that must all offer the same five theme modes and six colour presets** - a fix to the scheduler or the Stripe client has to reach Gmail, Sheets, Docs, the bundle and Browse Darkly in one commit rather than five repos (docs/project-story.md records the three-repo era where an 80% code overlap carried a 3x maintenance cost).
      
      A build-time CSS prefix loader rewrites `darkly-` to `gd-`/`sd-`/`dd-`/`ds-`/`bd-` so a customer can install a standalone extension and the bundle side by side; a `data-darkly-active` mutex on the html element then lets only the first loader claim the page.
    '''
    link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/README.md#L1-L100 "source"
    link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/package.json#L1-L56 "source"
    link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/pnpm-workspace.yaml "source"
    link https://darklysuite.com "site"
    api_licensing = container "Payment and licensing API (Pages Functions)" {
      technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, D1, Stripe REST API, Web Crypto, Google OAuth"
      summary "Cloudflare Pages Functions on darklysuite.com/api: Stripe checkout, webhook, token status, account/admin portals, D1 licence store."
      description '''
        The revenue backend. Authored once in `@darkly/landing-shared/functions` and mounted under `packages/landing-suite/functions`, running on the Cloudflare Workers runtime against a D1 database (`darkly-suite-db`).
        
        Endpoints: `/api/checkout` (creates a Stripe Checkout session for a product+plan pair), `/api/webhook` (verifies the Stripe signature with `crypto.subtle` HMAC-SHA256 and writes the licence), `/api/status/{token}` (licence check), `/api/portal` (Stripe billing portal), Google-OAuth `/api/auth/*`, `/api/account/*` for customers and `/api/admin/*` for licences, stats and discount codes.
        
        It resolves 15 Stripe price IDs from environment bindings (5 products x monthly/yearly/lifetime) **because the product line is sold as either a single-app licence or a Suite licence, and a `suite` licence must silently satisfy a status query for `gmail`, `sheets` or `docs` - that grant rule is the mechanism behind the bundle upsell**. CORS is limited to known extension IDs and a D1 sliding-window rate limiter caps requests per IP. Secrets (Stripe keys, webhook signing secret, Google OAuth client secret) come from Cloudflare bindings and are not stored in the repo.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/checkout.ts "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/webhook.ts "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/status/[token].ts "source"
      lsh__account_api = component "Account portal API" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, D1, Stripe billing portal"
        summary "Customer-facing session, subscriptions list and Stripe billing-portal redirect, authorised by a 7-day user_sessions cookie."
        description '''
          Serves the customer account portal named in the vision brief, because buyers who never created an account still need a way to see and manage what they bought. `requireUser` resolves the `darkly_user_session` cookie to an email, `subscriptions` returns every licence for that email joined to its discount code, and `portal` mints a Stripe billing-portal session — but only after verifying the requested `customer_id` belongs to a licence owned by that email, which is the ownership check that stops one customer opening another's billing portal.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/account/subscriptions.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/account/portal.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/account/session.ts "source"
        lsh__account_portal_file = file "account/portal.ts — ownership-checked billing portal" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Verifies the customer_id belongs to the session email before creating a Stripe billing portal session, else 403."
          description '''
            Delivers 'subscription management via the Stripe billing portal' from the vision brief while preventing horizontal privilege escalation, because customer ids are guessable identifiers passed from the browser.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/account/portal.ts#L1-L49 "source"
        }
        lsh__account_subs_file = file "account/subscriptions.ts" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Returns all licences for the signed-in email, newest first, with the discount code joined in."
          description '''
            Backs the one screen a paying customer actually visits, because a Suite buyer may hold several product rows and needs to see plan, status and expiry for each before deciding to manage billing.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/account/subscriptions.ts#L1-L52 "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__admin_api = component "Admin API (licences, stats, discount codes)" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, D1, Stripe REST"
        summary "ADMIN_EMAIL-gated routes for browsing/cancelling licences, per-product stats, and Stripe promotion-code CRUD; sessions validated against admin_sessions."
        description '''
          The solo operator's control surface, because a one-person commercial extension business needs licence lookup, revenue stats and discount codes without a separate SaaS. `requireAdmin` checks the `darkly_admin_session` cookie against a non-expired `admin_sessions` row on every route.
          
          Routes: list/search licences (deliberately POST-with-JSON-body; the GET variant returns 405 with an `Allow` header because admins search by customer email and PII in query strings lands in access logs), licence detail enriched best-effort with live Stripe subscription/customer data, DELETE/PATCH for cancelling subscriptions (immediately or at period end via the Stripe client), per-product and 30-day-signup stats aggregated in SQL, and discount codes which are read/written straight against Stripe promotion codes and coupons rather than D1 — Stripe's `times_redeemed` is treated as the source of truth.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/admin/licenses.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/admin/discount-codes.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/admin/stats.ts "source"
        lsh__admin_auth_file = file "admin/_shared/auth.ts — session guard" {
          technology "TypeScript, WebCrypto"
          summary "requireAdmin cookie/session check, cookie parser, and the 32-byte crypto-random session token generator shared by admin and account portals."
          description '''
            The single gate protecting every admin route, because the portal is guarded by ADMIN_EMAIL at login and by a D1 session row thereafter. Its `parseCookie` and `generateSessionToken` helpers are reused by the account portal and by the checkout email-prefill cookie, making this the de-facto session primitive for the whole backend.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/admin/_shared/auth.ts#L1-L51 "source"
        }
        lsh__admin_discounts_file = file "admin/discount-codes.ts — Stripe promo CRUD" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Lists, creates, edits and archives Stripe coupons/promotion codes, scoped to one product via coupon applies_to."
          description '''
            Implements the discount-code capability named in the vision brief by delegating to Stripe rather than D1, because Stripe already tracks redemptions natively; codes are generated from an ambiguity-free alphabet and can be restricted to a single Darkly product id through `getProductStripeId`.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/admin/discount-codes.ts#L1-L130 "source"
        }
        lsh__admin_licenses_file = file "admin/licenses.ts — search, cancel, patch" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "POST-body search with a sortable-column whitelist, plus DELETE/PATCH that cancel the Stripe subscription behind a licence."
          description '''
            The operator's main licence console endpoint, because supporting a paying knowledge worker means finding their row by email and cancelling or amending it. Two hardening details: sort columns come from a fixed whitelist to block SQL injection through column names, and the list operation is POST-only so customer emails never appear in a query string.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/admin/licenses.ts#L1-L160 "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__api_guardrails = component "CORS, rate limiting and request validation" {
        technology "TypeScript, Cloudflare D1"
        summary "Extension-ID allowlisted CORS, a D1-backed fixed-window rate limiter, and the Env/License types with UUID, plan and product validators."
        description '''
          The shared defence layer every public route composes, because the API is called cross-origin from Chrome extensions and from five marketing domains and must not become an open proxy to Stripe. `cors.ts` matches `chrome-extension://` origins against the 32-char ID pattern and the `ALLOWED_EXTENSION_IDS` allowlist, fails closed in production when unset, relaxes only when `ENVIRONMENT === 'development'`, and derives bare+www web origins from `SITE_URL` alongside the three Google app origins where the content scripts run.
          
          `rate-limit.ts` implements the D1 sliding/fixed window from the brief: a batched cleanup + upsert + read against `rate_limits(ip, endpoint, window_start)` keyed on `CF-Connecting-IP`, defaulting to 10 requests per 60 seconds and returning a `Retry-After`. `types.ts` holds the `Env` binding surface (D1, Stripe secrets, OAuth, ADMIN_EMAIL, per-product SITE_URLs, optional Resend key) plus `isValidToken`, which pins identity to a UUID v4 shape.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/cors.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/rate-limit.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/types.ts "source"
        lsh__cors_file = file "_shared/cors.ts" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Origin allowlist for the five marketing domains, the three Google app origins, and known Chrome extension IDs; fail-closed in production."
          description '''
            Directly implements 'CORS is restricted to known extension IDs' from the vision brief, because the licensing API is reachable from any origin and only the published CWS extension IDs plus Darkly's own sites should get a permissive header.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/cors.ts#L1-L99 "source"
        }
        lsh__env_types_file = file "_shared/types.ts — Env bindings and validators" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Declares every binding and secret name the backend expects, the License row shape, and isValidToken/isValidPlan/isValidProduct."
          description '''
            The contract between the code and the Cloudflare Pages environment, because the whole monetisation surface (15 price ids, 5 product ids, OAuth client, ADMIN_EMAIL, per-product site URLs, extension-ID allowlist) is configuration rather than code and this file is the authoritative list of the names to provision.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/types.ts#L1-L82 "source"
        }
        lsh__rate_limit_file = file "_shared/rate-limit.ts" {
          technology "TypeScript, D1 batch"
          summary "checkRateLimit batches cleanup + upsert + read against the rate_limits table; getClientIp reads CF-Connecting-IP."
          description '''
            The D1 sliding-window limiter named in the vision brief, because /api/status is polled by every installed extension and /api/checkout spends a Stripe API call per request, so both need a per-IP ceiling that survives across Workers isolates.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/rate-limit.ts#L35-L83 "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__auth_fn = component "Google OAuth start/callback" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, Google OAuth 2.0, JWT decode, D1"
        summary "One OAuth entry point multiplexing four flows via a state prefix: admin login, account-portal login, pre-checkout email capture, and purchase restore."
        description '''
          Backs every identity-bearing capability in the product because Google OAuth is the only login mechanism: the ADMIN_EMAIL-gated admin portal, the customer account portal, and the two token-related flows. `/api/auth/start` builds the consent URL (`openid email` scope only) and encodes the flow plus a 16-byte CSRF nonce into `state`, mirrored into an HttpOnly `darkly_oauth_state` cookie with a 10-minute lifetime.
          
          `/api/auth/callback` verifies state, exchanges the code, decodes the id_token (checking issuer, audience and expiry) and branches:
          - **checkout** — writes the verified email into a 5-minute HttpOnly cookie scoped to /api/checkout and redirects there, so Stripe gets the right email without PII in a URL.
          - **restore** — the reinstall path: looks up an active licence by email (product or 'suite') and repoints its `token` at the new extension token, so the extension's poller picks the licence up on its next /api/status call.
          - **user** — creates a 7-day `user_sessions` row only if that email owns at least one licence.
          - **admin** — rejects anything but ADMIN_EMAIL, creates a 24-hour `admin_sessions` row and notifies the operator by email.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/auth/start.ts#L1-L73 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/auth/callback.ts#L1-L267 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/google-oauth.ts "source"
        lsh__auth_callback_file = file "auth/callback.ts — four-flow OAuth callback" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "State-prefix router for admin / user / checkout / restore flows, including the licence-token repointing that restores a purchase after reinstall."
          description '''
            Concentrates the trust decisions for the whole suite because it is where a Google identity becomes either an admin session, a customer session, a Stripe prefill email, or a licence-token rebind. Note the deliberate skip of JWT signature verification, justified in-file by the token arriving directly from Google's token endpoint over HTTPS.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/auth/callback.ts#L18-L165 "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__checkout_fn = component "Checkout function (/api/checkout)" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, TypeScript, Stripe Checkout REST"
        summary "Validates UUID token + plan + product, resolves the Stripe price from the 5x3 price matrix, and 303-redirects the buyer to Stripe Checkout."
        description '''
          Pages Function that turns a click on a Pricing tier into a Stripe Checkout Session, because monetisation is one Stripe account with 5 products x 3 plans = 15 prices and this route is the only place that maps (product, plan) to a price id via `getPriceId`. It enforces the no-account-needed identity model: the buyer is identified solely by the UUID v4 token generated at install (`isValidToken`), which is stamped into Stripe session metadata as `{token, plan, product}` so the webhook can mint the licence row later.
          
          Security/UX behaviours worth mapping:
          - Rate limited to 10 req/60s per IP through the D1 sliding window, deliberately stricter than /api/status because each call hits the Stripe API.
          - Success/cancel URLs are per-product: a Gmail purchase returns to gmaildarkly.com (`SITE_URL_GMAIL`), a Browse purchase to browsedarkly.com, defaulting to darklysuite.com — this is what makes five separate marketing sites share one backend.
          - Email prefill arrives only via a short-lived HttpOnly cookie written by /api/auth/callback and is cleared on every exit path (success or error), so a verified email is never put in a query string and never leaks into a later checkout.
          - `lifetime` maps to Stripe mode `payment`, monthly/yearly to `subscription`.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/checkout.ts#L1-L161 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/__tests__/checkout.test.ts "source"
      }
      lsh__d1_schema = component "D1 licence schema" {
        technology "SQLite / Cloudflare D1"
        summary "Canonical schema for licenses, discount_codes(+usages), admin_sessions, user_sessions, rate_limits and webhook_events."
        description '''
          The single authoritative definition of the licence database that all of the Pages Functions run against, because production D1 must match it and a previously divergent copy in landing-suite was folded into this superset. Structurally it encodes several product rules: `UNIQUE(token, product)` makes the UUID token plus product the entitlement key (enabling the checkout upsert to be idempotent), `stripe_status` carries `past_due`/`cancel_at_period_end` for the warning banners, `idx_licenses_email` supports both the restore-purchase lookup and account-portal sign-in, `rate_limits` is the sliding-window table, and `webhook_events` is the Stripe redelivery dedup ledger. The file also carries the run-once migration statements as comments.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/d1/schema.sql#L1-L110 "source"
      }
      lsh__email_helper = component "Resend email notifier" {
        technology "TypeScript, Resend REST API"
        summary "Fire-and-forget plain-text sender used for operator alerts (purchases, cancellations, payment failures, admin logins) and user payment-recovery mail."
        description '''
          Implements the 'optional Resend email notifies the operator' capability, because a solo operator has no dashboard alerting and wants a mail on every purchase, cancellation-with-reason, payment failure and admin login. It no-ops entirely when `RESEND_API_KEY` is absent and swallows/logs all failures so a mail outage can never fail a webhook or an OAuth callback. Two senders are distinguished: notifications@ for operator alerts and admin@ for the customer-facing 'update your payment method' message.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/email.ts#L1-L72 "source"
      }
      lsh__functions_tests = component "Pages Functions test suite" {
        technology "Jest, ts-jest"
        summary "Jest/ts-jest suites covering webhook, checkout, status, auth, admin licences, discount codes, CORS, rate limiting, products and email."
        description '''
          The executable specification for the licensing backend, because the money path (Stripe events to D1 licence to /api/status unlock) has no staging user to catch regressions. The webhook suite alone is the largest file in the package and pins the idempotency ledger, ownership guards and both legacy/clover Stripe payload shapes; the CORS and status suites pin the extension-ID allowlist and the Suite-satisfies-any-product query.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/__tests__/webhook.test.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/__tests__/status.test.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/__tests__/cors.test.ts "source"
        lsh__webhook_test_file = file "__tests__/webhook.test.ts" {
          technology "Jest"
          summary "1300-line suite pinning signature verification, event dedup/reclaim, ownership guards and licence state transitions."
          description '''
            Guards the highest-consequence code in the suite, because a webhook regression either double-charges attention (duplicate emails) or silently fails to grant a licence someone paid for.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/__tests__/webhook.test.ts "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__status_fn = component "Extension-facing status and portal endpoints" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, D1, Stripe REST"
        summary "/api/status/{token} answers the licence query every extension polls; /api/portal deep-links a token holder into the Stripe billing portal."
        description '''
          The endpoint the five MV3 extensions call to decide whether to unlock, because identity is a UUID token in chrome.storage.sync and there is no account. The SQL implements the bundle upsell mechanism directly: `WHERE token = ? AND product IN (?, 'suite')` ordered so an exact product match wins and a Suite licence otherwise satisfies the query for any individual product.
          
          The JSON reply carries `paid`, `plan`, `product`, `expiresAt`, plus live Stripe display prices fetched best-effort via `getProductPrices` (so extensions can render current pricing without a redeploy), and `subscriptionStatus`/`cancelAt` only when there is a warning to show. Rate limited 10 req/60s per IP and wrapped in the extension-ID-restricted CORS helper, so a stolen token cannot be polled from an arbitrary origin. The sibling /api/portal route takes the same token, looks the licence up in D1 and returns a Stripe billing-portal URL, giving in-extension subscription management.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/status/[token].ts#L1-L102 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/portal.ts "source"
        lsh__status_portal_file = file "portal.ts — token-scoped billing portal" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Rate-limited, CORS-guarded route that exchanges an extension token for a Stripe billing portal session URL."
          description '''
            Lets a user manage or cancel a subscription from inside the extension without ever creating a Darkly account, because the token in chrome.storage.sync is the only identity the product has. Mirrors the checkout route's guardrail stack (extension-ID CORS + 10 req/60s D1 rate limit) since it too spends a Stripe API call per request.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/portal.ts#L1-L100 "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__stripe_client = component "Stripe client and product/price registry" {
        technology "TypeScript, Stripe REST v1, WebCrypto HMAC"
        summary "Dependency-free fetch wrapper over the Stripe REST API plus the (product, plan) to price-id map for all 15 prices and its reverse lookup."
        description '''
          The only place the backend talks to Stripe, because Workers runtimes favour a raw-fetch client over the Node SDK. Covers checkout sessions, session/price/subscription/customer retrieval, billing portal sessions, coupon and promotion-code CRUD, subscription cancellation (now and at period end), and constant-time-ish HMAC webhook signature verification via WebCrypto.
          
          `products.ts` is the monetisation registry that encodes 5 products x 3 plans = 15 Stripe prices as env vars, the per-product Stripe product ids used for coupon `applies_to`, the reverse price-id lookup that lets the webhook identify Darkly events when no D1 row exists, and `getProductPrices`, which fetches live prices so landing pages and extensions display real amounts without a redeploy. All Stripe credentials are env-injected secrets referenced by name only.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/stripe.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/products.ts "source"
        lsh__products_registry_file = file "_shared/products.ts — 15-price registry" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "getPriceId, getProductStripeId, getProductPlanFromPriceId and getProductPrices over the gmail/sheets/docs/suite/browse x monthly/yearly/lifetime matrix."
          description '''
            Encodes the entire commercial catalogue in one file, because the '5 products x 3 plans = 15 prices' model in the vision brief has to be resolvable in both directions: forward for checkout, reverse for webhook ownership guards when the D1 licence row is gone.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/products.ts#L1-L121 "source"
        }
        lsh__stripe_helper_file = file "_shared/stripe.ts" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "createCheckoutSession, createPortalSession, retrieve price/subscription/customer, promo-code CRUD, cancelSubscription, verifyWebhookSignature."
          description '''
            Single chokepoint for outbound Stripe calls, because every monetisation capability (checkout, billing portal, discounts, cancellation, webhook trust) routes through it and its signature verifier is what makes the webhook safe to expose publicly.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/_shared/stripe.ts#L1-L140 "source"
        }
      }
      lsh__webhook_fn = component "Stripe webhook (/api/webhook)" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, Stripe webhooks, D1"
        summary "Signature-verified Stripe event sink that writes/updates the D1 licence row and emails the operator on purchase, cancellation and payment failure."
        description '''
          The write side of the licence database, because a purchase only becomes an entitlement once Stripe confirms it. Handles `checkout.session.completed` (upsert into `licenses` keyed on UNIQUE(token, product)), `customer.subscription.updated`, `customer.subscription.deleted` and `invoice.payment_failed`.
          
          Design points the map should carry:
          - Idempotency: each `event.id` is claimed in the `webhook_events` table before processing; a duplicate delivery yields 0 changed rows and is acknowledged without re-running side effects. Claims older than 1 hour are reclaimable (orphaned-claim recovery); handler failure releases the claim so Stripe's retry re-processes; rows older than 30 days are pruned opportunistically.
          - Ownership guards: because the same Stripe account serves non-Darkly products, events are ignored unless the session metadata names a valid Darkly product or the subscription's price id reverse-maps through `getProductPlanFromPriceId`. Price extraction is shape-robust across the legacy `item.price.id` and the 2026-01-28.clover `item.pricing.price_details.price` shapes.
          - Grace period: `active`, `trialing` and `past_due` all keep the licence `active`; `past_due` and `cancel_at_period_end` are surfaced through `stripe_status` so the extension can show a warning banner rather than revoking access mid-retry.
          - Operator notification and a user 'update your payment method' email go out through the Resend helper.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-shared/functions/api/webhook.ts#L1-L500 "source"
      }
      lsuite__deploy_config = component "Wrangler / D1 / secrets deployment config" {
        technology "Wrangler, Cloudflare Pages, D1"
        summary "wrangler.toml binding the D1 licence database and sibling-site URLs, .env.example enumerating the 15 Stripe prices and OAuth secrets, and the retired local d1 schema."
        description '''
          Binds the deployed hub to its backing services, **because** the licence authority is only real once D1 is attached and the Stripe/OAuth secrets exist:
          
          - `wrangler.toml` declares `pages_build_output_dir = "dist"`, binds `DB` to the `darkly-suite-db` D1 database, and sets plaintext vars for `SITE_URL` plus the four sibling marketing domains (gmaildarkly / sheetsdarkly / docsdarkly / browsedarkly) so backend redirects can send a buyer back to whichever site referred them. A comment states all Stripe ids are production secrets, never committed.
          - `.env.example` documents the secret surface without values: Stripe secret + webhook signing secret, 15 price ids (5 products x monthly/yearly/lifetime), 5 product ids used for coupon `applies_to` restriction, Google OAuth client id/secret, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, an optional Resend key for operator notifications, and `ALLOWED_EXTENSION_IDS` — the comma-separated allowlist that drives the extension-ID CORS restriction in production.
          - `.dev.vars` holds local sandbox values and is gitignored.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/wrangler.toml#L1-L20 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/.env.example#L1-L49 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/d1/schema.sql "source"
        lsuite__file_d1_schema = file "d1/schema.sql (retired pointer)" {
          technology "SQL (retired)"
          summary "Tombstone file: the local copy was retired and the canonical D1 schema now lives in packages/landing-shared/d1/schema.sql."
          description '''
            Prevents schema drift in the licence database **because** a per-site copy had diverged in both directions (this copy lacked `licenses.stripe_status`, `idx_licenses_email`, `user_sessions` and `webhook_events`; the shared copy lacked `discount_code_usages` and the `discount_codes` active/max_uses/use_count columns); the two were reconciled into the shared file as the canonical superset and this file now only records that fact.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/d1/schema.sql#L1-L8 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_env_example = file ".env.example" {
          technology "dotenv template"
          summary "Documents every Pages secret: Stripe keys, 15 price ids, 5 product ids, Google OAuth, admin email, Resend key, extension-ID CORS allowlist."
          description '''
            The authoritative inventory of the monetisation surface **because** it is where the brief's "5 products x 3 plans = 15 prices" becomes concrete configuration, and where `ALLOWED_EXTENSION_IDS` — the CORS allowlist restricting `/api/status/{token}` to known extension origins — is declared. All values are placeholders; real values live only as Cloudflare Pages secrets.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/.env.example#L1-L49 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_wrangler_toml = file "wrangler.toml" {
          technology "Wrangler TOML"
          summary "Pages project config: dist output dir, D1 binding DB to darkly-suite-db, and SITE_URL vars for the hub plus four sibling sites."
          description '''
            The deployment contract for the licence authority **because** the `DB` binding is what gives every mounted Pages Function access to the shared licence/rate-limit tables, and the `SITE_URL_*` vars are how the backend knows the marketing-only sibling domains that funnel buyers to this checkout.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/wrangler.toml#L1-L20 "source"
        }
      }
      lsuite__functions_mount = component "Pages Functions mount (re-export layer)" {
        technology "Cloudflare Pages Functions, TypeScript re-exports"
        summary "16 one-line files under functions/api/** that re-export the shared handlers, turning file paths into the live API routes on darklysuite.com."
        description '''
          The layer that makes darklysuite.com the licence authority, **because** Cloudflare Pages routes by filesystem path: each file here is a single `export { onRequest* } from '@darkly/landing-shared/functions/api/...'` line, so the shared backend implementation is deployed once per site while the route surface is declared per package. Zero business logic lives in this package.
          
          Mounted surface: `/api/checkout`, `/api/webhook` (Stripe), `/api/portal` (billing portal), `/api/status/{token}` (the endpoint all five extensions poll, exporting `onRequestOptions` for the extension-ID CORS preflight), `/api/auth/start` + `/api/auth/callback` (Google OAuth), the admin set (`licenses`, `licenses/[id]`, `discount-codes`, `stats`, `session`, `logout`) and the account set (`session`, `subscriptions`, `portal`, `logout`). `tsconfig.functions.json` type-checks this directory against `@cloudflare/workers-types` separately from the SPA.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/status/[token].ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/checkout.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/webhook.ts "source"
        lsuite__file_fn_admin_licenses = file "functions/api/admin/licenses.ts" {
          technology "Pages Functions"
          summary "Mounts GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/admin/licenses for the operator's licence management console."
          description '''
            Gives the solo operator direct control of the licence database **because** the admin portal at `/admin/memberships` needs full CRUD over issued licences to handle refunds, comps and support escalations without touching D1 by hand.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/admin/licenses.ts#L1-L1 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_fn_auth_callback = file "functions/api/auth/callback.ts" {
          technology "Pages Functions, Google OAuth"
          summary "Mounts the Google OAuth redirect handler backing both the admin portal and the customer account portal."
          description '''
            Enables the two signed-in surfaces on the hub **because** the admin portal and the customer account portal are the only parts of darklysuite.com that need identity beyond the anonymous UUID token; the redirect URI is derived from the request origin at runtime per `.env.example`.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/auth/callback.ts#L1-L1 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_fn_checkout = file "functions/api/checkout.ts" {
          technology "Pages Functions"
          summary "Mounts GET/POST/OPTIONS /api/checkout, the Stripe Checkout session creator the SPA redirects to."
          description '''
            Closes the loop with the SPA **because** `CHECKOUT_API_URL` in `src/config.ts` points every pricing CTA at this same-origin path, which then creates the Stripe session for the chosen product+plan and the visitor's UUID token.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/checkout.ts#L1-L1 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_fn_status = file "functions/api/status/[token].ts" {
          technology "Pages Functions dynamic route"
          summary "Mounts GET/OPTIONS /api/status/{token} — the licence check every extension calls."
          description '''
            The single most load-bearing route in the package **because** all five MV3 extensions verify entitlement by calling `/api/status/{token}` and the Suite-satisfies-individual-product rule is resolved behind it; exporting `onRequestOptions` alongside `onRequestGet` is what allows the CORS preflight from known extension origins.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/status/[token].ts#L1-L1 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_fn_webhook = file "functions/api/webhook.ts" {
          technology "Pages Functions"
          summary "Mounts POST /api/webhook for Stripe events that write licences into D1."
          description '''
            The write path of the licence database **because** a purchase only becomes an entitlement when Stripe's event lands here and is persisted against the buyer's token; its signing secret is supplied as a Pages secret listed in `.env.example`.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/functions/api/webhook.ts#L1-L1 "source"
        }
        lsuite__file_tsconfig_functions = file "tsconfig.functions.json" {
          technology "TypeScript project references"
          summary "Workers-runtime TypeScript project for functions/, separate from the DOM-typed SPA project."
          description '''
            Keeps the two halves of the package honest **because** the API mount runs on the Workers runtime (`@cloudflare/workers-types`, no DOM lib) while the SPA runs in the browser; `pnpm type-check` runs both projects so a bad re-export fails before deploy.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-suite/tsconfig.functions.json#L1-L27 "source"
        }
      }
    }
    ext_browse = container "Browse Darkly (Chrome extension)" {
      technology "Chrome MV3, React 18, webpack, Chrome side panel API"
      summary "MV3 extension darkening every website via all-urls, with a Chrome side panel, popup, per-site memory and smart detection. v1.0.0."
      description '''
        The expansion product beyond Google Workspace, built from `@darkly/core` + `@darkly/site-generic`.
        
        Declares a `sidePanel` surface plus a popup and runs two content scripts at `document_start` - an isolated-world `content.js` and a MAIN-world `page-world.js` - **because darkening arbitrary sites before first paint (and reaching page-level styling that an isolated world cannot) is what delivers the "no white flash, per-site memory, smart detection" promise it competes with Dark Reader on**.
        
        Unlike the Workspace extensions it uses `externally_connectable` for darklysuite.com and browsedarkly.com rather than a `landing-bridge` content script, and takes `tabs`/`activeTab` permissions to drive per-tab state from the side panel. CSS prefix `bd`, storage key `bd_preferences`.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L47 "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/webpack.common.js#L18-L26 "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/package.json "source"
      ext__browse_background = component "Browse Darkly background service worker" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 service worker"
        summary "Custom worker: side-panel behaviour, payment client, checkout poller, and an external token handoff for landing pages."
        description '''
          The only product with a hand-written worker rather than `createBackgroundWorker`, because it owns side-panel logic the shared factory does not model: it enables the panel and sets `openPanelOnActionClick`, and opens it on `bd:openSidePanel` from either a tab or the popup. It runs `createPaymentClient(config)` and `createCheckoutPoller(config)` so `checkProStatus`/`getProStatus` resolve against the licence API, and its `onMessageExternal` handler returns the `bd_token` UUID to darklysuite.com and browsedarkly.com so Stripe checkout creates a licence bound to this install. On fresh install it opens the subscribe page with the token attached. An in-file comment records that alarm-driven schedule-mode updates are still deferred here.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/background.ts#L1-L117 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts#L1-L14 "source"
      }
      ext__browse_content = component "Browse Darkly universal content script" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 content script"
        summary "Runs at document_start on all-urls, defers to Workspace extensions and dark sites, then drives the GenericDarkMode engine."
        description '''
          The delivery point for the promise of dark mode on every other website, and the only content script that bypasses the `createContentScript`/SitePlugin model in favour of `GenericDarkMode` from `@darkly/site-generic`. Its precedence chain is the interesting part: it hard-defers on `mail.google.com`, `docs.google.com`, `sheets.google.com` and `drive.google.com` so the specialised Darkly products win, then honours the `data-darkly-active` mutex, then reads `bd_preferences`, `bd_domain_overrides` and `bd_blocklist` from `chrome.storage.local` and skips blocklisted domains and already-dark sites (via `isDarkSite()`) unless the user explicitly opted in. It then serves `bd:toggle`, `bd:getStatus` and `bd:setPreset` messages from the popup and side panel so preset changes apply live.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/content.ts#L1-L104 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts "source"
        ext__browse_manifest = file "Browse Darkly MV3 manifest" {
          technology "Chrome MV3 manifest"
          summary "all-urls content script plus MAIN-world script, sidePanel + tabs permissions, and externally_connectable landing domains."
          description '''
            The broadest permission surface of the five products because the value proposition is every website: all-urls host permission, a `side_panel.default_path` of `sidepanel.html` for the settings home, and `tabs`/`activeTab` so the panel can track the active domain for per-site overrides. Instead of a landing-bridge content script it uses `externally_connectable` for darklysuite.com and browsedarkly.com, letting those pages message the worker directly for the token handoff.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L47 "source"
        }
      }
      ext__browse_page_world = component "Browse Darkly page-world matchMedia shim" {
        technology "TypeScript, MAIN-world content script"
        summary "MAIN-world script at document_start that makes prefers-color-scheme report dark while the page is claimed."
        description '''
          Injected in the page's main world so it can monkey-patch `window.matchMedia`, which the isolated content-script world cannot reach. It exists because many modern sites branch their own styling on `prefers-color-scheme`, and a site that keeps serving its light stylesheet under Darkly's inversion filter produces washed-out results; by returning `matches: true` for dark queries only while `data-darkly-active` is present on the html element, the shim gets sites to hand over their own dark assets and reverts to native behaviour the moment Browse Darkly stands down.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/page-world.ts#L1-L31 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/static/manifest.json#L28-L33 "source"
      }
      ext__browse_sidepanel_ui = component "Browse Darkly side panel + popup UI" {
        technology "React 18, TypeScript, chrome.sidePanel"
        summary "React side panel with General/Themes/Advanced/Account sections, plus a minimal popup that toggles the current tab."
        description '''
          The Chrome side panel is Browse Darkly's answer to the vision's 'settings live where you work' rule for a product with no host app to embed into. `sidepanel.tsx` tracks the active tab's domain through `chrome.tabs` listeners, shows a Pro/Free badge from the core payment client with `onPaymentStatusChange` live updates, and hosts four collapsible sections: General (the five theme modes including schedule hours and sunrise/sunset), Themes (preset cards rendered from core `PRESETS` swatches, global or per-domain), Advanced (per-domain override and blocklist management) and Account (licence status, plan prices, manage-subscription). The popup is intentionally minimal: one toggle for the current domain plus an 'Open Settings' button that opens the panel.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/sidepanel.tsx#L1-L228 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/popup.tsx "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/sidepanel.html "source"
        ext__browse_account_section = file "AccountSection (licence + plans)" {
          technology "React, TypeScript"
          summary "Shows Pro/Free status, plan prices from the licensing API, upgrade CTA and manage-subscription link."
          description '''
            The in-extension face of the monetisation model: it builds a `createPaymentClient(config)` against `bd_token`/`bd_pro_cache` and the darklysuite.com API base, renders the licence state and `PriceInfo` plan options fetched for the browse product, and routes upgrade clicks into the checkout flow that the background worker's poller then confirms. It is what makes an entitlement bought on the marketing site visible inside the extension.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/components/AccountSection.tsx#L1-L70 "source"
        }
        ext__browse_advanced_section = file "AdvancedSection (per-site rules)" {
          technology "React, TypeScript"
          summary "Per-domain enable/preset overrides and the blocklist editor backed by bd_domain_overrides and bd_blocklist."
          description '''
            Provides the per-site memory that the Dark Reader/Night Eye audience expects: it edits `bd_domain_overrides` (enabled flag plus optional preset per hostname) and `bd_blocklist` in `chrome.storage.local`, the same two keys the content script consults at `document_start` before deciding whether to invert a page, so an exclusion takes effect on the next load without any further coordination.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/components/AdvancedSection.tsx#L100-L150 "source"
        }
        ext__browse_general_section = file "GeneralSection (five theme modes)" {
          technology "React, TypeScript"
          summary "Renders the dark/light/system/schedule/sunrise-sunset mode picker plus hour selectors, persisting to bd_preferences."
          description '''
            The clearest in-repo statement of the five-mode promise, with the mode list and per-mode copy defined inline and hour pickers formatted for schedule mode. It reads and writes `bd_preferences` in `chrome.storage.local` and imports `ThemeMode`, `ScheduleConfig`, `SunriseSunsetConfig` and `DEFAULT_PREFERENCES` from core so Browse Darkly's preference shape stays identical to the Workspace products.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/components/GeneralSection.tsx#L1-L34 "source"
        }
        ext__browse_themes_section = file "ThemesSection (colour presets)" {
          technology "React, TypeScript"
          summary "Preset grid built from core PRESETS and DEFAULT_DARK_VARIABLES, applied globally or as a per-domain override."
          description '''
            Implements the six-colour-preset capability for the general browsing audience: it renders swatches from `--darkly-bg-primary`, `--darkly-bg-secondary`, `--darkly-accent` and `--darkly-text-primary` for each preset, writes the choice to `bd_preferences` or to `bd_domain_overrides` when the user scopes it to the current site, and relies on the content script's `bd:setPreset` message to re-apply the engine without a reload.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/browse-darkly/src/components/ThemesSection.tsx#L1-L45 "source"
        }
      }
    }
    ext_docs = container "Darkly for Docs (Chrome extension)" {
      technology "Chrome MV3, React 18, webpack"
      summary "MV3 extension for docs.google.com/document with a Kix canvas observer, forceColorSchemeLight, and Preserve Page Colors. v1.0.0."
      description '''
        Standalone Docs product built from `@darkly/core` + `@darkly/site-docs`.
        
        Sets `forceColorSchemeLight` in its ProductConfig **because Google's own native Docs dark mode would otherwise fight the filter inversion and produce a double-darkened page, which would break the "Preserve Page Colors" capability that keeps document pages rendering in their true colours**.
        
        Observes `.kix-canvas-tile-content` for the document surface and injects its toolbar control via MutationObserver against the Docs app bar. CSS prefix `dd`, storage key `dd_preferences`. Scoped to the `/document/*` path so it does not collide with the Sheets extension on docs.google.com.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L42 "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/package.json "source"
      ext__docs_background = component "Docs background service worker" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 service worker"
        summary "Seven-line worker delegating to createBackgroundWorker(config) with the dd-schedule-check alarm and offscreen geolocation."
        description '''
          Identical in shape to the Sheets worker and equally thin, because the schedule/sunrise-sunset modes and the `/api/status/{token}` licence check are core capabilities parameterised only by `ProductConfig`. Its offscreen document supplies coordinates for the sunrise/sunset mode that a service worker cannot obtain itself.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/src/background.ts#L1-L7 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/src/offscreen.ts "source"
      }
      ext__docs_build = component "Docs webpack build + dd- prefixing" {
        technology "webpack 5, ts-loader"
        summary "Four-entry build aliasing @darkly/core and @darkly/site-docs, copying docs-overrides.css with darkly- to dd- rename."
        description '''
          Produces content, background, offscreen and the shared landing-bridge bundles, and rewrites every `darkly-` CSS token to `dd-` while copying `themes.css`, `docs-overrides.css` and `settings-panel.css`. That rename is what allows a user who owns both Darkly for Docs and the Suite bundle to install both without one extension's settings-panel styles bleeding into the other's.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/webpack.common.js#L1-L88 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/webpack.prod.js "source"
      }
      ext__docs_content = component "Docs content script entry" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 content script"
        summary "Guards iframes and print/export/preview paths, claims the page as 'dd', then composes core with the docs plugin."
        description '''
          Runs on `https://docs.google.com/document/*` and delivers the Docs product's injected toolbar settings button and 'Preserve Page Colors' behaviour through `docsPlugin`. It adds `/preview` to the Sheets-style skip list (alongside `/print` and `/export`) because inverted page colours must never leak into a printed or previewed document, and it refuses to run when `claimPage('dd')` reports the Suite bundle already owns the tab.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/src/content.ts#L1-L31 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/static/manifest.json#L11-L27 "source"
        ext__docs_config = file "Docs product config (forceColorSchemeLight)" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "ProductConfig with prefix 'dd' and the only standalone forceColorSchemeLight flag."
          description '''
            The one product config that sets `forceColorSchemeLight: true`, because Google Docs ships its own half-finished native dark theme and letting it engage underneath Darkly's `invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg)` filter would double-darken the page. Pinning the host app to light gives the filter a predictable input, which is what makes 'Preserve Page Colors' produce accurate document colours.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/docs-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts#L1-L15 "source"
        }
      }
    }
    ext_gmail = container "Darkly for Gmail (Chrome extension)" {
      technology "Chrome MV3, InboxSDK, React 18, webpack"
      summary "MV3 extension for mail.google.com using InboxSDK for a native sidebar settings panel and toolbar button. Published on CWS at 1.0.2."
      description '''
        The flagship and, per the README launch table, the only listing currently published (v1.0.2).
        
        Ships `background.js`, `content.js` and a web-accessible `pageWorld.js` **because InboxSDK under MV3 needs a page-world script to reach Gmail's proprietary DOM, which is what buys the native-feeling sidebar settings panel and toolbar button the product is sold on**. A separate `landing-bridge.js` content script runs on gmaildarkly.com and darklysuite.com so a purchase made on the web can hand its licence token back to the installed extension.
        
        Host permissions are deliberately narrow - mail.google.com for the product itself, darklysuite.com for licence status, api.sunrise-sunset.org for the sunrise/sunset schedule mode. CSS prefix `gd`, storage key `gd_preferences`, conflict claim id `gd`.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L43 "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/package.json "source"
      ext__gmail_background = component "Gmail background service worker" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 service worker"
        summary "Nine-line worker that loads the InboxSDK background handler and delegates everything to createBackgroundWorker(config)."
        description '''
          MV3 service worker registered as `background.js`. It imports `@inboxsdk/core/background.js` because InboxSDK needs its background half present to inject `pageWorld.js`, without which the in-Gmail settings sidebar silently fails; then it calls `createBackgroundWorker(config)` so schedule alarms, sunrise/sunset lookups, offscreen geolocation and licence-status polling all come from shared core code rather than per-product duplication. The paired offscreen document supplies `navigator.geolocation`, which service workers cannot use, and that is what makes the sunrise/sunset theme mode possible.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/background.ts#L1-L9 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/offscreen.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/offscreen.html "source"
        ext__gmail_offscreen = file "Offscreen geolocation document" {
          technology "Chrome offscreen document"
          summary "Answers 'get-geolocation' messages with lat/lng from navigator.geolocation and reports 'offscreen-ready'."
          description '''
            Exists because the sunrise/sunset theme mode needs the user's coordinates before it can call sunrise-sunset.org, and an MV3 service worker has no `navigator.geolocation`. The document is created by core's offscreen helper, answers one message type with a 10s timeout and 5-minute `maximumAge` cache, and returns an `{ error }` payload on denial so the extension can fall back to another mode instead of hanging. Near-identical copies ship in sheets-darkly, docs-darkly and darkly-suite.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/offscreen.ts#L1-L27 "source"
        }
      }
      ext__gmail_build = component "Gmail webpack build + CSS prefixing" {
        technology "webpack 5, ts-loader, copy-webpack-plugin"
        summary "Five-entry webpack build that aliases @darkly/core and @darkly/site-gmail and rewrites darkly- CSS tokens to gd-."
        description '''
          Defines the five bundles that make up the shipped extension (content, pageWorld, background, offscreen, landing-bridge) and resolves `@darkly/core` / `@darkly/site-gmail` straight to workspace source, which is the composition model the vision calls maintainer leverage. Its `transformPrefix` copy transform rewrites `.darkly-`, `--darkly-` and `data-darkly-` to the `gd-` namespace while copying `themes.css`, `gmail-overrides.css` and `settings-panel.css`, which is exactly the collision guard that lets the standalone Gmail extension and the Suite bundle run side by side. A licences plugin emits THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt for store review.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/webpack.common.js#L1-L89 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/webpack.prod.js "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/package.json "source"
        ext__gmail_webpack_entries = file "webpack.common.js entry + prefix transform" {
          technology "webpack config"
          summary "Entry map including the shared core landing-bridge, plus the darkly- to gd- transform applied to every copied stylesheet."
          description '''
            Worth calling out on its own because two vision-level mechanisms live in this file: the `landing-bridge` entry is resolved out of `../core/src/landing-bridge.ts` (so all four Workspace products share one checkout bridge), and `transformPrefix` is the build-time CSS namespace rename that prevents class collisions between a standalone extension and the bundle.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/webpack.common.js#L5-L24 "source"
        }
      }
      ext__gmail_content = component "Gmail content script entry" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 content script"
        summary "Thin entry that claims the page via data-darkly-active, then composes @darkly/core's content script with the gmail site plugin."
        description '''
          Content script injected at `document_end` on `https://mail.google.com/*` (with `styles/themes.css`, `styles/gmail-overrides.css`, `styles/settings-panel.css`). It exists because the Gmail product must deliver filter-based inversion plus the InboxSDK settings sidebar while coexisting with the Darkly Suite bundle: it first calls `claimPage('gd')` and bails out when another Darkly extension already owns the page, which is the `data-darkly-active` mutex described in the vision. Only after the claim succeeds does it call `createContentScript(config, gmailPlugin)`, so all theme-mode/preset logic stays in the shared core and this package stays a ~18-line wiring file.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/content.ts#L1-L18 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/static/manifest.json#L11-L27 "source"
        ext__gmail_config = file "Gmail product config (gd prefix)" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "ProductConfig literal binding productId 'gmail', CSS prefix 'gd', storage/token keys and the darklysuite.com API base."
          description '''
            Single source of per-product identity consumed by both the content script and the background worker. It matters because every collision-avoidance and monetisation mechanism in the vision keys off these values: `prefix: 'gd'` drives the build-time `darkly-` to `gd-` CSS rename and the page-claim id, `tokenKey: 'gd_token'` is the UUID identity stored in chrome storage, and `apiBase: 'https://darklysuite.com/api'` is where `/status/{token}` is queried so a Suite licence can satisfy the Gmail product check.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts#L1-L14 "source"
        }
        ext__gmail_manifest = file "Gmail MV3 manifest (v1.0.2)" {
          technology "Chrome MV3 manifest"
          summary "Declares the Gmail content script, landing-bridge script, InboxSDK page-world web-accessible resource, and the three host permissions."
          description '''
            The only manifest in the repo at version 1.0.2, matching the vision's note that Gmail is the single published CWS listing. It is the concrete permission contract for the product's capabilities: `storage`+`alarms` for the five theme modes and schedule checks, `offscreen`+`scripting` for geolocation and InboxSDK injection, and host permissions limited to `mail.google.com`, `darklysuite.com` (licence status) and `api.sunrise-sunset.org` (sunrise/sunset mode). It also registers `landing-bridge.js` on gmaildarkly.com and darklysuite.com so checkout can bind to the extension's token.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L43 "source"
        }
      }
      ext__gmail_pageworld = component "Gmail page-world script (InboxSDK)" {
        technology "TypeScript, InboxSDK page-world bundle"
        summary "Four-line MAIN-world bundle re-exporting @inboxsdk/core/pageWorld.js, exposed as a web-accessible resource."
        description '''
          Separate webpack entry emitted as `pageWorld.js` and listed under `web_accessible_resources` for `mail.google.com`. It is required because the vision's promise of settings living inside the host app is delivered in Gmail through an InboxSDK sidebar, and InboxSDK can only reach Gmail's own app state from the page's main world rather than the isolated content-script world. The source map is also declared web-accessible, which is why the CWS package ships `pageWorld.js.map`.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/src/pageWorld.ts#L1-L4 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/gmail-darkly/static/manifest.json#L28-L33 "source"
      }
    }
    ext_sheets = container "Darkly for Sheets (Chrome extension)" {
      technology "Chrome MV3, React 18, webpack"
      summary "MV3 extension for docs.google.com/spreadsheets with a Waffle grid observer and a Preserve Grid Colors toggle. v1.0.0, in development."
      description '''
        Standalone Sheets product built from `@darkly/core` + `@darkly/site-sheets`.
        
        Watches `#waffle-grid-container` and injects its toolbar button through a MutationObserver **because Sheets has no InboxSDK equivalent, and the paid feature here is the "Preserve Grid Colors" toggle that re-inverts the grid canvas so cell fills and text stay true under the page-wide filter inversion**.
        
        Matches only the `/spreadsheets/*` path of docs.google.com so it can coexist with the Docs extension on the same origin. CSS prefix `sd`, storage key `sd_preferences`. Also injects `landing-bridge.js` on sheetsdarkly.com and darklysuite.com to carry the licence token from checkout back into the extension.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L42 "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/package.json "source"
      ext__sheets_background = component "Sheets background service worker" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 service worker"
        summary "Seven-line worker delegating to createBackgroundWorker(config) with the sd-schedule-check alarm and offscreen geolocation."
        description '''
          Carries no Sheets-specific logic on purpose: because every product shares the same five theme modes, licence polling and alarm plumbing, the package only supplies its `ProductConfig` (prefix `sd`, alarm `sd-schedule-check`, token `sd_token`) and lets core own the behaviour. The paired offscreen document provides geolocation for sunrise/sunset mode.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/src/background.ts#L1-L7 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/src/offscreen.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts "source"
      }
      ext__sheets_build = component "Sheets webpack build + sd- prefixing" {
        technology "webpack 5, ts-loader"
        summary "Four-entry build aliasing @darkly/core and @darkly/site-sheets, copying sheets-overrides.css with darkly- to sd- rename."
        description '''
          Composes the product from `@darkly/core` plus the single `@darkly/site-sheets` plugin, matching the vision's one-core-plus-one-plugin model, and applies the `sd-` CSS namespace rename so the standalone Sheets extension cannot collide with the Suite bundle's `ds-` classes when both are installed. Entries are content, background, offscreen and the shared core landing-bridge; there is no page-world entry because Sheets needs no InboxSDK.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/webpack.common.js#L1-L88 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/webpack.prod.js "source"
      }
      ext__sheets_content = component "Sheets content script entry" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 content script"
        summary "Guards iframes, print/export views and the page-claim mutex before composing core with the sheets plugin."
        description '''
          Runs on `https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/*` and is the delivery point for the Sheets product's toolbar settings button and 'Preserve Grid Colors' behaviour, which are supplied by `sheetsPlugin`. Three explicit guards run before `createContentScript`: it skips when `window.self !== window.top` so embedded spreadsheets are not inverted twice, it skips `/print` and `/export` paths so exported output keeps true colours, and it skips when `claimPage('sd')` fails because the Suite bundle already claimed the page.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/src/content.ts#L1-L30 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/src/darkly.config.ts "source"
        ext__sheets_manifest = file "Sheets MV3 manifest" {
          technology "Chrome MV3 manifest"
          summary "Spreadsheet-scoped content script with sheets-overrides.css, landing bridge on sheetsdarkly.com, no scripting permission."
          description '''
            Encodes the narrower surface the Sheets product needs: unlike Gmail it requests no `scripting` permission and exposes no page-world resource, because the Sheets settings entry point is an injected toolbar button rather than an InboxSDK sidebar. It still carries `alarms`+`offscreen` for schedule and sunrise/sunset modes and the `darklysuite.com` host permission for `/api/status/{token}` licence checks, and registers the landing bridge on both sheetsdarkly.com and darklysuite.com so either marketing site can start a bound checkout.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/sheets-darkly/static/manifest.json#L1-L43 "source"
        }
      }
    }
    ext_suite_bundle = container "Darkly Suite bundle (Chrome extension)" {
      technology "Chrome MV3, InboxSDK, React 18, webpack"
      summary "One MV3 extension covering Gmail, Sheets, Docs and Drive with four content scripts and a single routing background worker. v1.0.0."
      description '''
        The upsell SKU, published as package `darkly-suite-ext`.
        
        Depends on `@darkly/core` plus all four site plugins and ships `content-gmail.js`, `content-sheets.js`, `content-docs.js` and `content-drive.js` behind one background service worker that routes messages and alarms by URL - **it bundles the Gmail theme engine, the Sheets Waffle observer and the Docs Kix observer together because the suite sells one licence covering all Workspace apps, and the backend grants any single-product status query from a `suite` licence**.
        
        Keeps per-site preferences (`ds_gmail_preferences`, `ds_sheets_preferences`, `ds_docs_preferences`) and uses per-site prefixes for theme CSS while reserving `ds-` for UI components and storage keys, so override CSS written for the standalone products works unchanged. Conflict claim ids `ds-gmail`/`ds-sheets`/`ds-docs` stop double-injection when a standalone extension is also installed. Drive support ships as a content script whose plugin (`@darkly/site-drive`) the README describes as a stub for future work.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/static/manifest.json#L1-L68 "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/package.json "source"
      ext__suite_background = component "Suite unified background service worker" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 service worker"
        summary "Builds four site workers but registers one message/alarm/install listener set, routing by sender tab URL."
        description '''
          Custom 213-line worker rather than four `createBackgroundWorker` calls, because registering N duplicate Chrome listeners in one MV3 service worker would double-handle every message. It creates a `createSiteWorker` per site, routes `getScheduleStatus`/`getSunTimes` by parsing the sender tab URL into a `SiteId`, and answers shared `getProStatus`/`getLocation`/`getToken` from a single shared worker since all four sites share one token and one licence. Sun-time requests are latitude/longitude range-validated before reaching the sunrise/sunset lookup. On install it opens `darklysuite.com/subscribe?token=...&amp;product=suite` and immediately starts the checkout poller so a purchase completed in the web tab flips the extension to Pro without a restart.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/src/background.ts#L1-L213 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/src/offscreen.ts "source"
      }
      ext__suite_build = component "Suite webpack build + ds- prefixing" {
        technology "webpack 5, ts-loader, copy-webpack-plugin"
        summary "Eight-entry build aliasing core plus four site plugins, copying every override stylesheet with darkly- to ds- rename."
        description '''
          The widest build in the repo: four content bundles, background, offscreen, pageWorld and the shared landing-bridge, with aliases to `@darkly/site-gmail`, `-sheets`, `-docs` and `-drive`. It demonstrates the composition claim in the vision literally, since the bundle is core plus four plugins and no bespoke theming code. Its `transformPrefix` rewrites all `darkly-` tokens to `ds-`, giving the bundle a namespace distinct from `gd-`/`sd-`/`dd-` so the bundle and any standalone extension can be installed together.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/webpack.common.js#L1-L108 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/webpack.prod.js "source"
        ext__suite_manifest = file "Suite MV3 manifest (4 sites)" {
          technology "Chrome MV3 manifest"
          summary "Four host-scoped content script blocks with per-site override CSS, a landing bridge block, and page-world resources."
          description '''
            Shows how one listing covers four Google apps: separate `content_scripts` entries scope `content-gmail.js`, `content-sheets.js`, `content-docs.js` and `content-drive.js` to `mail.google.com`, `docs.google.com/spreadsheets`, `docs.google.com/document` and `drive.google.com`, each with its own override stylesheet plus the shared `themes.css`/`settings-panel.css`. It requests `offscreen` and `alarms` for geolocation-driven sunrise/sunset and schedule modes, and exposes `pageWorld.js` to all three Google hosts for InboxSDK.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/static/manifest.json#L1-L68 "source"
        }
      }
      ext__suite_content_scripts = component "Suite per-site content scripts (4)" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 content scripts"
        summary "content-gmail/sheets/docs/drive entries, each claiming a distinct ds-site page id and composing core with its site plugin."
        description '''
          Four separate bundles, one per host app, which is how the bundle delivers Gmail, Sheets, Docs and Drive from a single CWS listing. Each claims a site-scoped id (`ds-gmail`, `ds-sheets`, `ds-docs`, `ds-drive`) through the `data-darkly-active` mutex so it stands down when the matching standalone extension has already claimed the tab, and each resolves its own `ds_site_preferences` storage key via `getSiteConfig`, so a user can run dark Gmail and light Sheets from one install. The Sheets, Docs and Drive scripts skip iframes and Sheets/Docs additionally skip print/export/preview paths to protect exported colour accuracy. A four-line `pageWorld.ts` re-export ships alongside for InboxSDK on Gmail.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/src/content-gmail.ts#L1-L30 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/src/content-sheets.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/src/content-docs.ts "source"
        ext__suite_site_config = file "Suite config + getSiteConfig()" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Suite-level ProductConfig plus a per-site table that derives storage key, alarm name and URL pattern for each of the four sites."
          description '''
            The hinge of the bundle upsell: `getSiteConfig(siteId)` returns a full `ProductConfig` that keeps the suite's shared `ds_token`, `ds_pro_cache` and `darklysuite.com` API base (so one Suite licence answers every product status query) while swapping in per-site preferences and alarms. It also pins the unified `ds` CSS prefix because the bundle's stylesheets are compiled with `ds-` at build time, and sets `forceColorSchemeLight` for docs and drive to stop Google's own dark theme fighting the inversion filter.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/src/darkly.config.ts#L1-L78 "source"
        }
      }
      ext__suite_landing_bridge = component "Landing bridge content script (shared)" {
        technology "TypeScript, Chrome MV3 content script"
        summary "Runs on landing domains, hands the extension's UUID token to the page via CustomEvents, and forwards checkout completion."
        description '''
          Built from `packages/core/src/landing-bridge.ts` into darkly-suite, gmail-darkly, sheets-darkly and docs-darkly, and registered in each manifest against that product's marketing domain plus darklysuite.com. It is the mechanism that binds a Stripe checkout to the right licence row: it asks the background worker for `getToken`, dispatches `darkly-extension-token` to the page (re-dispatching on `darkly-token-request` when the page loads after the script), and forwards the page's `darkly-checkout-complete` event back as a `checkoutComplete` message that starts the poller. It deliberately uses `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` with no extension id so it works for unpacked builds during development as well as published listings.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/core/src/landing-bridge.ts#L1-L43 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/darkly-suite/static/manifest.json#L43-L47 "source"
      }
    }
    tool_screenshot_harness = container "Screenshot harness (asset pipeline)" {
      technology "TypeScript, tsx, Playwright, React 18, sharp, YAML"
      summary "Playwright + React + sharp pipeline that renders synthetic Gmail/Sheets/Docs pages and composites store-ready marketing screenshots."
      description '''
        A runnable Node/tsx pipeline (`pnpm build:pages`, `pnpm generate`) that renders fake Gmail inbox/compose/reading, Sheets spreadsheet and Docs document pages with faker-generated content, drives them in Playwright, and composites gradients, device frames and text overlays with sharp from YAML config.
        
        It is part of the product rather than incidental tooling **because every Chrome Web Store listing and landing page needs 1280x800 screenshots showing the extension's panel open in a real-looking Google app, and shipping five listings means regenerating that artwork per product without ever exposing the maintainer's real mail, spreadsheets or documents**.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/package.json "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/generate.ts "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/build-pages.ts "source"
      shot__capture = component "Playwright headless capture stage" {
        technology "Playwright 1.48 (Chromium, headless)"
        summary "Launches headless Chromium per shot, loads the mock page over file://, sets data-darkly-* attributes, injects theme CSS, waits for fonts, returns a 2x PNG buffer."
        description '''
          `captureScreenshot` is the only browser-driving code in the YAML pipeline. It resolves a page path to a `file://` URL (or passes http(s) through), launches `chromium` headless, opens a context at 1280x800 with `deviceScaleFactor: 2`, navigates with `waitUntil: 'networkidle'`, applies the `data-darkly-theme`/`data-darkly-preset` attributes via `page.evaluate`, injects each preset stylesheet with `page.addStyleTag`, awaits `document.fonts.ready`, pauses 200ms for rendering to settle, and returns a viewport-only PNG `Buffer`. It retries up to twice with 500ms/1000ms backoff, closing the browser on every path. Exists **because** the marketing screenshots must be rendered by a real browser at retina density for the Chrome Web Store's 1280x800 slots, and the retry loop keeps a flaky font load from breaking a bulk regeneration run.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/capture.ts "source"
      }
      shot__composite = component "sharp compositing stage" {
        technology "sharp 0.33 (libvips), generated SVG"
        summary "Layers gradient background, blurred drop shadow, macOS browser chrome, corner-masked screenshot and SVG title/subtitle into the final 1280x800 PNG."
        description '''
          `compositeScreenshot` turns a raw browser capture into finished marketing art. It computes a fixed layout (20px top padding, 60px text band, 40px chrome bar, 60px side padding, 45px bottom), renders an SVG linear gradient via `gradients.ts` (CSS-degree angles converted to SVG coordinates), resizes the capture into the content box, applies SVG masks so the chrome bar gets rounded top corners and the screenshot rounded bottom corners (flush seam between them), builds a shadow by blurring a rounded black rect, generates a macOS title bar with traffic lights and a URL pill from `frames.ts` (`macos-dark`/`macos-light`), renders XML-escaped title/subtitle text from `text-overlay.ts`, and composites all layers onto the gradient base. Exists **because** a bare app screenshot does not sell a listing — the Chrome Web Store tiles and landing heroes need a framed, captioned, gradient-backed image, and doing it in sharp means the operator regenerates polished artwork per product with one command.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/composite.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/gradients.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/frames.ts "source"
        shot__f_composite = file "pipeline/composite.ts" {
          technology "TypeScript, sharp"
          summary "Seven-step layering: gradient base, resized capture, corner masks, chrome frame, blurred shadow, text SVG, final sharp composite."
          description '''
            Holds the `LAYOUT` constants that define the visual identity of every generated store image and the SVG mask helpers. Significant **because** changing one constant here restyles the artwork for all five products at once.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/composite.ts#L27-L324 "source"
        }
        shot__f_frames = file "pipeline/frames.ts — macOS browser chrome SVG" {
          technology "TypeScript, SVG"
          summary "generateBrowserChrome(): macOS title bar SVG with red/yellow/green traffic lights and an address-bar pill, in dark and light styles."
          description '''
            Produces the device-frame illusion that makes a mock page read as a real browser tab at mail.google.com or docs.google.com. Significant **because** the address bar text comes from the YAML `browserUrl`, which is how a synthetic page is made to look like the genuine Google Workspace URL in store artwork.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/frames.ts#L29-L60 "source"
        }
      }
      shot__config_orchestrator = component "YAML config layer + generate orchestrator" {
        technology "TypeScript, tsx, yaml (v2)"
        summary "Per-product YAML declares each store shot (page, theme, preset, gradient, title, browser URL); generate.ts validates it and drives capture then composite then PNG."
        description '''
          The declarative front door of the harness. Each marketing product gets one YAML file (`config/gmail.yaml`, `config/sheets.yaml`, `config/docs.yaml`, plus `*-quick.yaml` smoke variants) listing screenshot definitions: `id`, `page`, `theme`, `preset`, marketing `title`/`subtitle`, two-stop `gradient`, `browserUrl`, and `injectCss` paths. `src/pipeline/generate.ts` parses the YAML, hard-validates required fields, resolves page and CSS paths relative to the config dir, then for each shot calls Playwright capture and sharp compositing and writes `output/extension/id.png`. Output size is pinned to 1280x800 (`OUTPUT_SIZE`) with a comment naming it the CWS standard, and a `--parallel` flag runs all shots concurrently. This exists **because** the solo operator must regenerate a full Chrome Web Store screenshot set per product (five listings, only Gmail published at 1.0.2) by editing a text file rather than hand-driving a design tool — the YAML is the per-product artwork spec.
          
          `src/types.ts` holds the whole contract: `ScreenshotConfig`/`ScreenshotDefinition` for the YAML schema, plus `CaptureOptions` and `CompositeOptions` for the two downstream stages.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/generate.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/types.ts "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/config/gmail.yaml "source"
        shot__f_cfg_gmail = file "config/gmail.yaml — Gmail listing shot set" {
          technology "YAML"
          summary "Five-shot spec for gmail-darkly: inbox dark, inbox Nord, reading dark, compose Monokai, inbox Catppuccin, each with its own gradient and mail.google.com URL bar."
          description '''
            The artwork spec for the one published listing. Each entry pairs a mock page with a theme/preset and a gradient tuned to that palette (e.g. the Nord shot on a matching muted-blue background) and stamps `mail.google.com` into the fake address bar. Listed **because** it is the concrete example of how one Chrome Web Store listing's five screenshots are described end-to-end in text.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/config/gmail.yaml#L1-L61 "source"
        }
        shot__f_generate = file "generate.ts pipeline entry point" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "CLI entry: loads/validates YAML, resolves pages and CSS, captures at 2x, composites to 1280x800, writes output PNGs."
          description '''
            Entry point run as `pnpm generate config.yaml [--parallel]`. `loadConfig` throws on a missing `extension`, an empty `screenshots` array, or a shot missing `id`/`page`/`title`/a 2-colour `gradient`, so a malformed artwork spec fails before Chromium launches. `processScreenshot` maps `theme`/`preset` onto the `data-darkly-theme` and `data-darkly-preset` HTML attributes the mock pages and injected CSS key off, captures at `deviceScaleFactor: 2`, then composites with fixed presentation defaults (12px radius, shadow on, 60px padding). Included **because** it is the single command that turns a product's YAML into the 1280x800 PNGs a Chrome Web Store listing and landing page need.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/pipeline/generate.ts#L26-L191 "source"
        }
        shot__f_types = file "types.ts — YAML schema and stage contracts" {
          technology "TypeScript"
          summary "Defines ScreenshotConfig/ScreenshotDefinition (the YAML schema), CaptureOptions, CompositeOptions, FrameStyle and the six-name PresetName union."
          description '''
            Single source of truth for the harness contract, split into mock-component types (Layout/Sidebar/GoogleHeader/InjectionSlot props, `SiteConfig`) and pipeline types (`CaptureOptions`, `FrameOptions`, `TextOverlayConfig`, `CompositeOptions`, `ScreenshotDefinition`, `ScreenshotConfig`). `PresetName` enumerates default/nord/solarized/monokai/catppuccin/rose-pine, matching the preset CSS files. Significant **because** every YAML field the operator can write to shape store artwork is declared here, so the schema is discoverable without reading the generator.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/types.ts#L73-L191 "source"
        }
      }
      shot__live_landing_capture = component "Live-extension landing capture scripts" {
        technology "Node ESM, Playwright (headed, launchPersistentContext), ImageMagick via execSync"
        summary "Standalone .mjs scripts that load the unpacked Sheets/Docs extensions into headed Chromium, drive real Google Docs/Sheets, open the settings panel and copy composites into the landing sites."
        description '''
          A second, parallel path that bypasses the synthetic-page pipeline entirely. `capture-sheets-landing.mjs` and `capture-docs-landing.mjs` launch a persistent Chromium context with `--load-extension` pointed at the built Sheets/Docs dist directories, sign into Google, create a real spreadsheet or document, type in scripted sample data, dismiss Google's own popups, wait for the extension's `data-darkly-active` attribute, flip light/dark with `page.emulateMedia({ colorScheme })` because the extension defaults to system mode, then screenshot clean light, clean dark, panel-open, cropped settings modal, gear-icon guide, and one panel per mode. Finished images are assembled with ImageMagick via `execSync` into `split-view.jpg` and a 2x2 `panel-views.jpg`, then copied into the landing-sheets and landing-docs public image directories. Exists **because** the landing pages need proof shots of the real extension's settings panel inside genuine Google Workspace, which the synthetic mocks cannot supply.
          
          Security note: both scripts hardcode a plaintext Google account username and password as module constants (values deliberately not reproduced here); ImageMagick is shelled out to but is not a declared dependency.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/capture-sheets-landing.mjs "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/capture-docs-landing.mjs "source"
        shot__f_capture_docs_landing = file "capture-docs-landing.mjs" {
          technology "Node ESM, Playwright"
          summary "708-line Docs twin of the Sheets script, targeting #dd-* selectors in docs-darkly/dist and writing into landing-docs public images."
          description '''
            Near-duplicate of the Sheets script with the `dd-` selector prefix and Docs-specific document setup. Significant **because** the duplication (including the duplicated hardcoded credentials and ImageMagick calls) is the maintenance cost of covering a second landing site, and any fix must be applied twice.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/capture-docs-landing.mjs#L1-L45 "source"
        }
        shot__f_capture_sheets_landing = file "capture-sheets-landing.mjs" {
          technology "Node ESM, Playwright"
          summary "666-line script: loads sheets-darkly/dist, builds a real 'Q1 Budget Planning' sheet, captures six #sd-* panel states, composites and copies into landing-sheets."
          description '''
            Documents the Sheets extension's live DOM contract in its header comment (`#sd-toolbar-button`, `#sd-sidebar-icon`, `.sd-mini-panel`, `.sd-modal-backdrop`) and encodes exact target image dimensions matching the landing placeholders. Significant **because** it is the only artefact that ties sheetsdarkly.com's hero and setup images to concrete selectors in the shipped extension — those selectors changing silently breaks artwork regeneration. Also the file carrying the hardcoded Google credentials.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/capture-sheets-landing.mjs#L1-L140 "source"
        }
      }
      shot__mock_pages = component "Synthetic Gmail/Sheets/Docs page renderers" {
        technology "Static HTML/CSS, React 18 + ReactDOMServer, @faker-js/faker (seeded)"
        summary "Hand-authored 1280-wide HTML clones of Gmail inbox/reading/compose, a Sheets spreadsheet and a Docs document, plus a React SSR builder and a seeded faker fixture module."
        description '''
          The fake Google Workspace surfaces that stand in for real user data. Two generations coexist: (1) committed static pages under `pages/` — `gmail/inbox.html`, `gmail/reading.html`, `gmail/compose.html`, `sheets/spreadsheet.html` ("Q1 Budget Planning"), `docs/document.html` ("Q1 Marketing Strategy") — each opening with `data-darkly-theme="light" data-darkly-active="true"` so injected Darkly CSS behaves as it would with the real extension loaded; and (2) a React server-side renderer, `src/build-pages.ts`, which composes `Layout` + `GoogleHeader` + `Sidebar` + `CompanionStrip` + `InjectionSlot` from a `SiteConfig` (only `sites/gmail.config.ts` is registered) and writes generated inbox HTML with token CSS inlined. `InjectionSlot` reproduces InboxSDK's `inboxsdk__appButton` markup so the extension's toolbar affordance appears in frame. `src/fixtures/base.ts` seeds faker at 42 and supplies deterministic avatar colours/initials. This exists **because** every CWS listing and landing page needs a screenshot of the settings panel inside a real-looking Google app, and shipping fake mail, spreadsheets and documents keeps real correspondence out of public store artwork.
          
          Accuracy note: `fixtures/base.ts` is currently imported by nothing — the committed HTML pages carry hardcoded sample content, so faker plumbing is present but unused.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/pages/gmail/inbox.html "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/pages/gmail/reading.html "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/pages/gmail/compose.html "source"
        shot__f_build_pages = file "build-pages.ts — React SSR mock page builder" {
          technology "TypeScript, React 18, ReactDOMServer"
          summary "Renders SiteConfig-driven Layout to static markup with ReactDOMServer, inlines token CSS and a reset, writes generated inbox HTML."
          description '''
            The programmatic alternative to the hand-written pages: one `SiteConfig` per Google product describes header, sidebar items and companion strip, and `ReactDOMServer.renderToStaticMarkup` emits a self-contained HTML file tagged `data-darkly-product`. Only `gmailConfig` is wired into the `SITES` array today. Significant **because** it is the intended path to add a new product's mock surface without authoring another 900-line HTML file by hand.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/src/build-pages.ts#L1-L120 "source"
        }
        shot__f_inbox_html = file "pages/gmail/inbox.html — synthetic Gmail inbox" {
          technology "HTML/CSS"
          summary "727-line standalone Gmail inbox clone: category tabs, message rows with senders/subjects/snippets, sidebar and toolbar, styled off --gw-* variables."
          description '''
            The most-used capture target — three of the five Gmail store shots point at it. Built entirely from `--gw-*` CSS custom properties so a single injected stylesheet can repaint it dark, and seeded with invented correspondence. Significant **because** it is the surface Chrome Web Store shoppers see in the only published listing, and no real inbox is ever involved.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/pages/gmail/inbox.html#L1-L40 "source"
        }
        shot__f_spreadsheet_html = file "pages/sheets/spreadsheet.html — synthetic Sheets grid" {
          technology "HTML/CSS"
          summary "1284-line fake 'Q1 Budget Planning' spreadsheet with formula bar, column/row headers, grid cells and sheet tabs."
          description '''
            The Sheets capture target, the largest mock page in the harness. Matters **because** Sheets artwork must show a dense, believable grid for dark mode to look convincing, and a synthetic budget sheet does that without exposing any real financial data.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/pages/sheets/spreadsheet.html#L1-L12 "source"
        }
      }
      shot__theme_css = component "Injectable Darkly theme + preset CSS" {
        technology "CSS custom properties"
        summary "darkly-dark.css maps --darkly-* tokens onto the mock pages' --gw-* variables; five preset files (Nord, Solarized, Monokai, Catppuccin, Rose Pine) override the palette."
        description '''
          The stylesheet bundle that makes a light mock page look like the shipped product. `css/darkly-dark.css` (696 lines) declares the canonical dark palette as `--darkly-*` custom properties — its header comments say the values are sourced from `@darkly/core` `themes.css` — and maps them onto the `--gw-*` variables the Gmail/Docs mocks use, with hardcoded class overrides for the Sheets mock. Each file under `css/presets/` re-declares only the `--darkly-*` values, so injecting `darkly-dark.css` then `nord.css` cascades the Nord palette through the whole page. YAML shots select these via `injectCss` and Playwright applies them with `page.addStyleTag`. Exists **because** the store artwork has to demonstrate the actual dark themes and preset palettes users buy, and re-implementing the extension's colours as an injectable sheet avoids loading the MV3 extension for the synthetic-page path.
          
          Risk worth mapping: these are hand-copied duplicates of the extension core's theme tokens, so palettes can drift from what ships.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/css/darkly-dark.css "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/css/presets/nord.css "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/css/presets/catppuccin.css "source"
        shot__f_darkly_dark_css = file "css/darkly-dark.css — injectable dark theme" {
          technology "CSS"
          summary "Declares the canonical --darkly-* dark palette and maps it onto Gmail/Docs --gw-* variables plus Sheets class overrides."
          description '''
            The base sheet every dark shot injects. Its `:root` block is the palette and the rest wires those tokens into mock-page selectors so a single injection repaints inbox, spreadsheet and document. Significant **because** it is the file that determines what "dark mode" looks like in every published screenshot.
          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/screenshot-harness/css/darkly-dark.css#L1-L40 "source"
        }
      }
    }
    web_browsedarkly = container "browsedarkly.com (Browse Darkly site)" {
      technology "Vite 7, React 19, Cloudflare Pages"
      summary "Vite + React 19 marketing site for Browse Darkly, configured as Cloudflare Pages project browse-darkly-landing."
      description '''
        Landing site for the general-web product.
        
        It is a separate property **because Browse Darkly competes for a different audience than the Workspace SKUs - the Dark Reader/Night Eye switcher described in docs/browse-darkly-plan.md - and needs positioning around performance, curated presets and privacy rather than around Gmail**. The Browse Darkly manifest lists this domain in `externally_connectable`, so the site can talk to the installed extension directly for setup and licence handoff instead of via an injected bridge script.
      '''
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-browse/package.json "source"
      link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-browse/wrangler.toml "source"
      link https://browsedarkly.com "site"
      lmkt__browse_ops_console_routes = component "Admin + account routes on browsedarkly.com" {
        technology "react-router-dom 7, @darkly/landing-shared admin/account components"
        summary "browsedarkly.com uniquely mounts shared AdminLayout/Licenses/Discounts/Stats and Account login/subscriptions routes; the other three sites do not."
        description '''
          `landing-browse/src/App.tsx` mounts `/admin`, `/admin/memberships`, `/admin/discounts`, `/admin/stats` behind `AdminLayout` and `/account`, `/account/subscriptions` behind `AccountLayout`, all imported from `@darkly/landing-shared`. This matters because it gives the solo operator a licence-administration and customer self-service console on a second origin beyond darklysuite.com, and it is the only one of the four per-product marketing sites to do so — the Gmail/Sheets/Docs sites instead link out to `https://darklysuite.com/account` from their nav. These routes talk to the licensing API for licence lookup, discount management and revenue stats rather than to any Browse-Darkly-specific backend.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-browse/src/App.tsx#L20-L29 "source"
      }
      lmkt__browse_site_app = component "browsedarkly.com SPA (landing-browse)" {
        technology "Vite 7, React 19, react-router-dom 7, TypeScript, lucide-react"
        summary "Vite+React SPA for browsedarkly.com targeting the general web reader: presets, smart detection, per-site memory; no screenshot gallery yet."
        description '''
          Marketing domain for **Browse Darkly**, the product aimed at the second audience — the general browser user currently served by Dark Reader/Night Eye — rather than the Workspace buyer. Its `HomePage` differs most from the three Workspace sites: two stacked `Features` blocks (curated presets Nord/Solarized/Monokai, smart already-dark detection, per-site theme memory, Chrome Side Panel settings; then OS sync, sunset, schedule, zero-telemetry) and a `Hero` with **no** screenshots array, because `public/images/` does not yet exist in this package.
          
          Routes are `/`, `/privacy`, `/success`, `/subscribe`, and a bespoke `/support` page (the Workspace sites have `/setup` instead) with a support contact and inline FAQ. `STORE_URL` is `PLACEHOLDER_BROWSE_ID` since the listing is unpublished, so `NAV_CTA` points at `/#pricing`. Checkout uses the same centralised `https://darklysuite.com/api/checkout`, and `useExtensionToken('browse')` picks the licence token up from the extension — the vision's externally_connectable path for Browse Darkly.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-browse/src/pages/HomePage.tsx#L63-L105 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-browse/src/config.ts#L1-L40 "source"
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/landing-browse/src/App.tsx#L10-L19 "source"
        lmkt__browse_config = file "landing-browse config.ts" {
