      siteng__sheets_plugin = component "Sheets site plugin (@darkly/site-sheets)" {
        technology "TypeScript, React 18, MutationObserver, chrome.storage.sync"
        summary "SitePlugin for spreadsheets: injected toolbar/sidebar buttons, Waffle-grid MutationObserver re-injection, and the Preserve Grid Colors toggle."
        description '''
          Google Sheets has no plugin SDK, so this package hand-injects UI into `#docs-header-container` and the companion app-switcher strip, then guards it with a debounced MutationObserver that re-injects whenever Sheets rebuilds its toolbar on sheet switch, resize or SPA navigation. `getPageContext()` distinguishes an editor URL (`/spreadsheets/d/{id}`) from the dashboard so the shared core can choose toolbar vs FAB placement. Its differentiating capability is Preserve Grid Colors from the vision brief: `SheetsSettingsSection` persists `{preserveGridColors}` under `${prefix}_site_sheets` in chrome.storage.sync, sets `data-&lt;prefix&gt;-grid="preserve"` on the html element, and `sheets-overrides.css` re-inverts `#waffle-grid-container canvas` plus the three frozen-pane canvases so cell fills stay chromatically accurate under whole-page inversion — the reason a spreadsheet user can trust conditional formatting in dark mode. `plugin.ts.init()` re-reads that stored flag on every page load so the preference survives navigation, and `renderProductSection()` hands the toggle to core's settings shell. Colour-picker swatch selectors are centralised in `dom-selectors.ts` alongside the grid and frozen-pane selectors, keeping every brittle Google class name in one auditable file.
        '''
        link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/site-sheets/src/plugin.ts#L22-L75 "source"
        siteng__sheets_grid_observer = file "inject/grid-observer.ts" {
          technology "MutationObserver"
          summary "Document-wide MutationObserver, 500 ms debounce; fires re-injection when the toolbar exists but the Darkly button is gone."
          description '''
            Keeps the injected toolbar button alive across Sheets' frequent toolbar rebuilds, because the brief's promise of in-app settings buttons fails visibly the moment Google re-renders its header and nothing puts the button back.
