      siteng__docs_plugin = component "Docs site plugin (@darkly/site-docs)" {
        technology "TypeScript, MutationObserver"
        summary "SitePlugin for Google Docs: Kix canvas observation, pageless-mode detection fed to the theme engine, injected toolbar/sidebar buttons."
        description '''
          Mirrors the Sheets injection approach for `https://docs.google.com/document/*` but its Docs-specific job is the Kix rendering surface. `detectPagelessMode()` inspects `.kix-appview-editor` for the `kix-appview-editor-pageless` class (or the absence of `.kix-page`) and pushes the result into core via `engine.setPagelessMode()`, because paginated and pageless documents need different background treatment under inversion. `canvas-observer.ts` is the same debounced re-injection guard as Sheets, watching for toolbar rebuild on view switch or SPA navigation. `docs-overrides.css` carries the Preserve Page Colors rules named in the brief: `data-darkly-page="preserve"` re-inverts `.kix-canvas-tile-content` and `.kix-page` so document pages stay light while chrome stays dark, and also re-inverts colour-picker swatches so the palette shows true colours. `dom-selectors.ts` additionally centralises collaboration-cursor (`.kix-cursor`) and comment/suggestion (`.docos-*`) selectors. Unlike Sheets there is no `ui/` settings section in this package, so the Preserve Page Colors CSS exists without a shipped toggle (see open questions) — the store-assets e2e plans in packages/docs-darkly and packages/darkly-suite explicitly treat the missing toggle as a known non-blocker.
