          '''
          link https://github.com/lucasmccomb/darkly-suite/blob/8816bd58e92a79f97dace48e5bd70955bf49b111/packages/site-docs/src/inject/dom-selectors.ts#L1-L54 "source"
        }
      }
      siteng__drive_plugin = component "Drive site plugin (@darkly/site-drive)" {
        technology "TypeScript, CSS"
        summary "Deliberately minimal dashboard-only plugin: no toolbar injection, no observer; CSS inversion plus icon/thumbnail re-inversion carries the whole feature."
        description '''
          The thinnest of the five site packages and effectively a stub: `drivePlugin` returns `'dashboard'` from `getPageContext()` (Drive has no editor mode), no-ops `injectToolbarButton` because dashboard surfaces use core's floating action button instead, and no-ops `startDomObserver` for the same reason. Only keyboard shortcuts (Alt+Shift chords) and `drive-overrides.css` are real. This exists because Drive ships only inside ext_suite_bundle — it is the bundle's fourth surface and part of the Suite upsell in the brief, not a standalone CWS listing — so the maintainer-leverage argument favours letting shared core handle UI and keeping the package to selectors plus CSS. The stylesheet does the substantive work: body inversion with media re-inversion, and explicit re-inversion of Drive's colour-coded file-type icons and thumbnails so a Docs file still reads blue and a Sheets file green after inversion. `dom-selectors.ts` records header, file-list, nav and search selectors for future use even though CSS currently handles the transformation without them.
