      lsh__account_portal_ui = component "Account portal UI" {
        technology "React 19, react-router-dom"
        summary "Customer-facing Google-login page, auth context, layout and a subscriptions table that links out to the Stripe billing portal."
        description '''
          The customer half of the portal capability in the vision brief, because someone who bought with nothing but a UUID token still needs a way to see what they own and change their card. `AccountAuthProvider` probes /api/account/session for `{authenticated, email}`, the login page sends the visitor to /api/auth/start?type=user, and the subscriptions page lists every licence for that email with product, plan, status badge, created/expiry dates and a manage-billing link that hits the ownership-checked /api/account/portal route. It deliberately reuses the admin stylesheet, so the portal ships without a third design system.
        '''
